<id/06/0695/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Liquorice"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "the roots of *Glycyrrhiza glabra*, a perennial plant common in the south of Europe, considerable quantities of which are imported. Liquorice is much used in the Levant in making a decoction which is drunk cold in summer, and liquorice water is a favourite beverage in this country with children. *See GOONCH. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 242]"@en ;
